WEBVTT

00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:08,560
Hello, Dr. Kevin Connors with your man bird me into the day.

00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,560
Today we're going to talk about cancer and sugar.

00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:15,560
I have a confession to make.

00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,560
I love sugar.

00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,560
Who doesn't love sugar?

00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,560
I remember when I was a little kid.

00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,560
My dad used to feed me a little packet of sugar.

00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,560
We were at a restaurant, which wasn't very often.

00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,560
But he thought he was being a really good dad.

00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,560
I put a little packet of sugar on a spoon and give it to me.

00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,560
I want him to say, dick!

00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,560
Don't do that.

00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,560
I loved it.

00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,560
I thought my dad was great.

00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:36,560
But he was creating an addiction in me, right?

00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:37,560
Sugar is not bad for you.

00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,560
It's not good for you and it feeds cancer.

00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,560
So what does cancer again?

00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:44,560
It's this rapidly replicating cell line.

00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:49,560
So rapidly replicating cell lines have a huge metabolic demand.

00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:51,560
They need fuel.

00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:55,560
It's rapidly replicating that just doesn't do that for free.

00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,560
It needs gasoline.

00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:02,560
Cancer is fueled by glucose.

00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:05,560
So that's why you look at a book.

00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:08,560
It talks about limiting your glucose levels.

00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,560
Limiting your carb levels.

00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:14,560
So carbohydrates, everything you eat can be broken down to glucose.

00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:17,560
But the things that are rapidly broken down to glucose are carbohydrates.

00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:22,560
The things that are really rapidly broken down to glucose are simple carbohydrates.

00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:25,560
And things that have what are called a high glycemic index.

00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,560
Even potatoes.

00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:30,560
Potatoes actually break down to glucose faster than table sugar does.

00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:37,560
So your starchy vegetables and your sugars are things that you have to eliminate

00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,560
when you have cancer.

00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,560
Or you were just feeding the cancer.

00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:47,560
So I know you crave these things but you have to limit those things.

00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:50,560
Now I do know that using a nursing approach and you're juicing vegetables

00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:53,560
that tends to be a lot of glucose.

00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,560
But you're getting a lot of enzymes with it.

00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,560
So when you're getting a lot of enzymes with it,

00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,560
you're kind of counteracting that glucose balance.

00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:03,560
So it's more than just limiting your carbs.

00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,560
So we don't want to get that wrong.

00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:08,560
But in our office, we test people on all the food.

00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:13,560
So we want to know exactly what that person can't eat and can't eat because it's very important.

00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:17,560
Because not all cancers are fed by the diet.

00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:21,560
So we have patients that come in that are used to eating at McDonald's

00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,560
and used to eating, you know, candy and cookies all day long.

00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,560
And then we have patients that have just a fantastic diet.

00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,560
And they typically want to go, why did I get cancer?

00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,560
Well, sometimes it has less to do with your diet.

00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,560
Everybody's completely different.

00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,560
And even though in my book, I have a standard diet protocol.

00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,560
That's just a standard diet protocol.

00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,560
It's a good one to follow.

00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:45,560
In general, cancer feeds is fed by glucose.

00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:48,560
So it's a high metabolic demand.

00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,560
It just gobbles up glucose.

00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:53,560
So you've got to stay away from sugar.

